# The packed library tarball IS committed, and it has to be.
#
# `package.json` depends on `@realwired/ui` as `file:vendor/realwired-ui-0.1.0.tgz`.
# Vercel runs `npm install` against a clean checkout, so if the tarball is not in
# the repo the install fails and there is no build — the dependency simply is not
# resolvable. 654 KB of binary in git is the price of the prototype deploying at
# all, and `npm run relink` will overwrite it in place each time the library moves.
#
# The alternative is publishing @realwired/ui to a registry and giving Vercel a
# token. Worth doing when the library has consumers outside this desktop; not
# before the 16th.

# Internal working documents — kept on disk, deliberately not in this repo.
#
# The published repo is public, and these are our own planning and engagement
# notes rather than part of the application. They stay in the working copy, so
# an agent working here still reads CLAUDE.md for its context.
CLAUDE.md
docs/PLAN.md
